From: Lili Cui <lili.cui@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 00:05:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] x86: Increase generic tune branch misprediction cost

Increase the branch misprediction cost factor for generic tuning from
COSTS_N_INSNS (2) to COSTS_N_INSNS (2) + 3 in ix86_max_noce_ifcvt_seq_cost.

Modern CPUs have deeper pipelines, making branch mispredictions more
expensive. Increasing this cost raises the if-conversion threshold,
encouraging replacement of branches with conditional moves (CMOV),
avoiding pipeline stalls from mispredicted branches.

This is a backport adaptation for GCC 12.3.0 where br_mispredict_scale
does not exist as a cost table field; the equivalent hardcoded value
COSTS_N_INSNS (2) in ix86_max_noce_ifcvt_seq_cost is modified directly.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/i386/i386.cc (ix86_max_noce_ifcvt_seq_cost): Increase
	branch misprediction cost from COSTS_N_INSNS (2) to
	COSTS_N_INSNS (2) + 3.
---
--- a/src/gcc/config/i386/i386.cc
+++ b/src/gcc/config/i386/i386.cc
@@ -23038,7 +23038,7 @@
 	return param_max_rtl_if_conversion_unpredictable_cost;
     }
 
-  return BRANCH_COST (true, predictable_p) * COSTS_N_INSNS (2);
+  return BRANCH_COST (true, predictable_p) * (COSTS_N_INSNS (2) + 3);
 }
 
